Classically, $\frac{d}{dt}\,\mathrm{Vol}_{\Gamma}=0,$ for a phase-space region transported by Hamiltonian flow. Quantum mechanically, $\begin{aligned}
\ket{\psi(t)}&=U(t)\ket{\psi(0)},\\
U^\dagger U&=I,\\
\braket{\psi(t)}{\phi(t)}
&=\braket{\psi(0)}{\phi(0)}.
\end{aligned}$ These are precise forms of the claim that microscopic distinctions survive time evolution.

